    "instagram:post": {
      "caption": {
        "body": "Taken around 1936 in a Douglas DC-3, this promotional TWA (Transcontinental \u0026 Western Air) photo advertises their complimentary meal service. At the time, these planes held up to 21 passengers and cruised at 175–200 miles per hour. The DC-3 was unpressurized and flew at lower altitudes than modern pressurized jetliners, usually below 10,000 feet. In spite of often flying around stormy weather, DC-3 flights still encountered plenty of turbulence at these altitudes. Though the food looks delicious, air sickness occurred frequently.  Image: Transcontinental \u0026 Western Air (TWA), Douglas DC-3, c. 1936.  Gift of TWA Clipped Wings International, Inc. 2002.113.334",
